        "content": {
          "Prompt": {
            "prompt": "ok sure but before that , i do want to i want to create this and experience this \nThe VCS-Driven Workflow:\n\n1. Edit code in Git repo (NOT in UI!)\n   ↓\n2. Open Pull Request\n   ↓\n3. HCP Terraform automatically runs plan\n   ↓\n4. Review plan in PR comments\n   ↓\n5. Merge PR to main branch\n   ↓\n6. HCP Terraform runs apply (if auto-apply enabled)\n   OR\n   Approve apply manually in HCP Terraform UI\n\n\nReal-Life Analogy: \nIt's like submitting a building permit - you submit plans (PR), city reviews them (plan), you get approval, then construction begins (apply)! 🏗️📋\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n\n## **Why VCS-Driven, Not UI-Driven?**\n\n| VCS-Driven (Correct) | UI-Driven (Wrong) |\n|-------------------------|----------------------|\n| Code lives in Git | Code lives in UI |\n| Version controlled | No version history |\n| Code review via PR | No review process |\n| Team collaboration | Single person |\n| Audit trail | Limited tracking |\n| CI/CD integration | Manual process |\n\nThe Correct Workflow:\n\nhcl\n# Step 1: Add resource in your Git repo (main.tf)\nresource \"aws_instance\" \"new_server\" {\n  ami           = \"ami-12345\"\n  instance_type = \"t2.micro\"\n  \n  tags = {\n    Name = \"new-server\"\n  }\n}\n\n\nbash\n# Step 2: Create feature branch and PR\ngit checkout -b feature/add-new-server\ngit add main.tf\ngit commit -m \"feat: add new server\"\ngit push origin feature/add-new-server\n\n# Open PR on GitHub/GitLab\n\n\n# Step 3: HCP Terraform automatically:\n- Detects the PR\n- Runs terraform plan\n- Posts plan results as PR comment\n- Shows what will be created/changed/destroyed\n\n\n# Step 4: Review and merge\n- Team reviews the plan in PR\n- Approve PR\n- Merge to main branch\n\n\n# Step 5: HCP Terraform automatically:\n- Detects merge to main\n- Runs terraform apply (or waits for manual approval)\n- Infrastructure is created\n### 🌍 Real-Life Application:\n\nProduction Scenario: At Netflix:\n\nDeveloper wants to add new EC2 instance:\n\n1. Creates feature branch: feature/add-cache-server\n2. Adds resource to main.tf\n3. Opens PR on GitHub\n4. HCP Terraform runs plan automatically\n5. Plan shows: \"1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy\"\n6. Team reviews plan in PR comments\n7. Senior engineer approves PR\n8. PR merged to main\n9. HCP Terraform applies changes\n10. New server is created\n11. Full audit trail in Git history\n\n\nBenefits:\n- **Version control** - Every change tracked in Git\n- **Code review** - Team reviews before apply\n- **Rollback** - Can revert Git commits\n- **Audit trail** - Who changed what, when\n- **Collaboration** - Multiple people can work safely\n- **Policy checks** - Sentinel policies run automatically, please suggest i can do same for this repo/ directory"
